 "about_text": "Clockshop is a nonprofit arts organization based in the Elysian Valley/Frogtown neighborhood of Los Angeles, founded in 2004 by filmmaker Julia Meltzer. Rather than running a conventional exhibition space, it commissions artists to create site-specific, experimental projects on public land, especially along the LA River at the Bowtie Parcel and at Los Angeles State Historic Park, in long-term partnership with California State Parks. Its program combines artist commissions, publications, and public programming with environmental and community advocacy, focusing on equitable green space, local history, and the relationship between artists, communities, and public lands throughout the LA River watershed.",
